flowchart TB
  accTitle: ENS402 shared provider resolver model
  accDescr: Platform and provider registries route service names to one shared resolver per provider. Each service has a separate record bundle. Ops and Treasury Admin have distinct key-scoped writer roles across all bundles.
  platform["Platform Registry"]
  provider["Provider Registry: provider.ens402.eth"]
  platform -->|provider subregistry| provider
  provider --> s1["service1"]
  provider --> s2["service2"]
  provider --> s3["service3"]
  s1 --> shared["Shared PermissionedResolver"]
  s2 --> shared
  s3 --> shared
  shared --> b1["Bundle 1: endpoint, description, price, payTo 1"]
  shared --> b2["Bundle 2: endpoint, description, price, payTo 2"]
  shared --> b3["Bundle 3: endpoint, description, price, payTo 3"]
  admin["Provider Admin: root ROLE_SET_TEXT + ROLE_SET_TEXT_ADMIN"] -.-> shared
  ops["Ops: ROLE_SET_TEXT on endpoint, description, avatar"] -.-> shared
  safe["Treasury Admin / Safe: ROLE_SET_TEXT on ens402.payment"] -.-> shared
  registrar["Authorized shared-service registrar: native ROLE_REGISTRAR"] -.-> provider
  registrar -.->|initialize five keys for new bundles| shared
  note["Key grants cover all service bundles. Treasury Admin is a job title, not an EAC admin grant. Real Safe configuration and public setup require verification."]
